+The implemented identity pairs cream paper, dark ink and forest-green actions with embedded Fraunces headings and a native Arial body. Pages use readable editorial spacing, quiet rules and restrained rounded surfaces. All public copy remains English.
+
+The established commercial landing keeps its photo-led asymmetric hero, explicit €9 offer stamp, strong request action, three-step purchase journey and readable report preview. The guide at `/seo-geo-audit` extends this identity as a single-column reading page, reusing the existing header, footer and actions. No framework or dependency was added.
+
+**Key Characteristics:**
+
+- Cream-paper background, forest-green actions and dark-ink text.
+- Fraunces headings paired with native Arial body text.
+- Shared responsive navigation and visible keyboard focus.
+- A commercial landing and a quieter guide using the same visual system.
+
+## Colors
+
+The frontmatter records the implemented CSS palette. The roles below refer to those same source values. The header request action and offer stamp use literal white text. No additional palette or tonal ramp is introduced for the guide.
+
+### Primary
+
+- **Forest Green** (#245440): actions and keyboard focus.
+- **Deep Forest Hover** (#234537): header request-action hover fill.
+
+### Neutral
+
+- **Cream Paper** (#f6f4ed): page background.
+- **Dark Ink** (#202c26): body text and primary-button hover fill.
+- **Muted Ink** (#515d55): supporting copy and helper text.
+- **Pale Botanical Tint** (#e6ebe1): tags, prompt and status blocks.
+- **Paper Rule** (#ccd1c5): borders and dividers.
+- **Warm White** (#fffef9): form/report surfaces and primary-button text.
+- **Error Red** (#8c2626): error text.
+
+## Typography
+
+**Display Font:** Fraunces (with Georgia, serif)
+
+**Body Font:** Arial (with Helvetica, sans-serif)
+
+**Character:** Embedded Fraunces supplies the editorial heading voice; native sans-serif keeps explanations and controls direct. The shared font uses `font-display: swap`, and headings use balanced wrapping.
+
+### Hierarchy
+
+- **Display** (400, 42–68px, line-height 1.08): the landing hero retains its fluid heading and short line length.
+- **Headline** (400, 30–44px, line-height 1.16): shared landing section headings.
+- **Guide Display** (400, 40–60px, line-height 1.08): fluid guide heading capped at (21ch).
+- **Guide Headline** (400, 28–36px, line-height 1.16): guide sections capped at (28ch), with (52px) above and (16px) below.
+- **Body** (16px, line-height 1.6): default interface copy; shared paragraphs are capped at (68ch).
+- **Guide Body** (18px, line-height 1.75): article paragraphs and ordered lists capped at (70ch).
+- **Label** (600, 15px): explicit form-field labels.
+- **Small** (13px): metadata, helper text and scope boundaries.
+
+The report filename bar and prompt use native monospace text, at (12px) and (13px) respectively.
+
+## Layout
+
+The shared header, main and footer are centered within (1200px), with desktop gutters of (32px). At (800px) and below, gutters become (20px), landing grids and the journey stack, the sticky example introduction becomes static and the footer stacks. At (480px) and below, the header wraps, navigation fills its own row and action-group primary buttons fill the available width.
+
+The landing retains its asymmetric two-column hero, responsive studio photograph and three-step journey. The guide uses a main shell capped at (900px), fluid block padding (40–72px), one article and body text capped at (70ch). Its real ordered questions retain native numbering, list padding of (24px), item padding of (6px) and vertical item margins of (18px). Final actions have (32px) above them.
+
+The guide shares the existing responsive header. Navigation links lead to `/seo-geo-audit`, `/#example` and `/#request`; the guide's final actions lead to `/#request` and the explicitly labelled fictional report at `/example.md`.
+
+## Elevation & Depth
+
+Paper color, warm-white containers and thin rules supply most depth. The report preview is flat: its final CSS override removes the earlier shadow. The form retains its implemented subtle shadow. The guide adds no shadows or raised cards.
+
+- **Form** (`box-shadow: 0 12px 36px #202c260a`): subtle separation beneath the existing request form.
+
+## Shapes
+
+Controls and prompt blocks use the control radius; report, form, studio photograph and offer stamp use the surface radius. The illustrative tag uses the smaller tag radius. Straight thin rules separate content; guide copy sits directly on the paper background.
+
+## Components
+
+### Buttons and links
+
+Filled forest-green buttons use warm-white text, semibold type and a minimum height of (48px). The landing hero adds padding of (16px 24px). Hover changes the primary fill to dark ink. Text actions remain underlined, with a minimum height of (44px). Source links retain descriptive labels and an underline offset of (4px). Background/color transitions last (.18s) with `ease`; reduced-motion preferences disable transitions. Disabled buttons use a wait cursor and opacity (.6).
+
+### Report and form
+
+The report keeps its filename bar, illustrative-example tag, separated findings and tinted monospace prompt. Required URL/email fields use explicit labels, helper text, a consent checkbox and a full-width submit action. Fields are (52px) high; hover darkens their rule border to muted ink. Status has a live region. Keyboard focus uses a forest-green outline (3px) with an offset of (5px), shared with links, buttons and disclosure summaries.
+
+### Navigation
+
+The shared header pairs a bold Audit GEO wordmark with underlined links and a filled request action. The supporting brand phrase disappears at the smaller breakpoint; the narrowest breakpoint gives navigation its own row. The skip link becomes visible on focus and targets main content.
+
+### Guide article
+
+One H1, publication metadata, descriptive H2s, ordinary paragraphs and four numbered questions form the article. Source links name the Google and OpenAI documentation. The hypothetical crawler-block example stays explicitly hypothetical. The closing eligibility-check action, labelled fictional report and privacy/scope link keep their established destinations. No imagery or motion is added to the guide.
+
+### Landing photograph
+
+Preserve the existing illustrative studio photograph, aspect ratio (14/11), alt text and explicit dimensions. Two embedded JPEG sizes (700px and 1400px) are served same-origin. Existing attribution: solidpixels, Unsplash photo `iq2RzBMj-Wg`, published 21 November 2021; [photo](https://unsplash.com/photos/a-laptop-computer-sitting-on-top-of-a-wooden-table-iq2RzBMj-Wg) and [license](https://unsplash.com/license). It illustrates a studio, with no customer endorsement or animation.
+
+## Do's and Don'ts
+
+### Do:
+
+- Do preserve the cream-paper/forest identity, Fraunces headings and native Arial body.
+- Do keep the shared responsive header and visible focus treatments on the guide.
+- Do use the implemented guide shell, line lengths, heading sizes and native numbered questions.
+- Do label source links descriptively and identify fictional examples explicitly.
+- Do keep English copy, the €9 one-off offer, eligibility and payment boundaries visible.
+
+### Don't:
+
+- Don't add a separate guide identity, imagery or motion to this reading-page extension.
+- Don't fabricate testimonials, conversion statistics, customer results or ranking promises.
+- Don't equate crawler eligibility with measured search position or consumer AI visibility.
+- Don't imply that submitting a request charges the visitor or bypasses eligibility and delivery-capacity review.
+- Don't promise email notifications or an included managed weekly service from the current public page.
