+const GUIDE=html("<main id=\"main\" class=\"guide\"><article><h1>What can an SEO/GEO audit actually prove?</h1><p class=\"small\">Published <time datetime=\"2026-10-14\">14 October 2026</time></p><p>A website check can show an observable barrier or a clearer next step. It cannot establish search rankings or AI recommendations from crawler access alone. Separate the evidence you can inspect today from the outcomes you need to measure over time.</p>\n<h2>Start with access, then check outcomes</h2><p>Google says pages supporting AI Overviews or AI Mode must be indexed and eligible for a search snippet. Meeting those requirements does not guarantee crawling, indexing or appearance. Its existing SEO foundations still apply; there is no special AI schema requirement. See <a href=\"https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features\">Google’s AI features guidance</a>.</p><p>OpenAI distinguishes OAI-SearchBot, used for search discovery, from GPTBot, used for potential training. Treat their policies separately. Allowing a search crawler is an access decision, not proof that your business will be cited. See <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/bots\">OpenAI’s crawler documentation</a>.</p>\n<h2>Four questions to ask before paying for an audit</h2><ol><li><strong>What was actually collected?</strong> Ask for sampled URLs, dates and relevant excerpts. An unavailable response is unknown. A collector size limit is a collection limitation, not a website defect.</li><li><strong>Does each proposed task follow from its evidence?</strong> A title can describe the wrong offer; an intentional crawler block can be correct. Ask which observation supports the change and when you should leave the page alone.</li><li><strong>What would count as a successful fix?</strong> Define a reproducible check: the intended directive is present, the title describes the verified offer, or the proposed copy matches actual capabilities.</li><li><strong>Which outcomes remain unmeasured?</strong> A technical fix and a customer acquisition result need separate evidence. Ask for denominators and dates before accepting a percentage improvement.</li></ol>\n<h2>A small example: an intentional crawler block</h2><p>Suppose a sampled robots.txt blocks a search crawler. The observation supports checking the owner’s policy. It does not automatically support removing the block. If search discovery is intended, inspect the matching crawler group and hosting controls before proposing a targeted change. If the block is intentional, make no change. This is a hypothetical example, not a customer finding.</p>\n<h2>Measure the result at the right level</h2><p>First reproduce the changed page or directive. For Google search outcomes, compare dated Search Console data over declared periods; Google includes its AI search features in overall Web performance reporting. That aggregate does not isolate an AI-only uplift. For an AI mention check, record the engine, interface, date and prompt sample, retain the actual responses, and report observed mentions over the number of checks. Treat a small sample as a sample, not a universal visibility score.</p>\n<h2>What our €9 pilot covers</h2><p>We sample public HTTPS pages using their initial HTML and check observable foundations and content. JavaScript rendering, search position measurement and consumer AI mention testing are not included in the current collection. A useful report provides up to three supported tasks, sources, verification steps and a prompt for your own agent. If the evidence does not support useful work, we do not invite payment.</p><p>Requests are open. A paid order depends on a reviewed useful report and confirmed delivery capacity. Save your private status page; email notifications are not currently promised.</p><div class=\"actions\"><a class=\"button\" href=\"/#request\">Request an eligibility check</a><a class=\"text-action\" href=\"/example.md\">Read the fictional report example</a></div><p class=\"small\">No ranking, citation or revenue guarantee. <a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy and scope</a></p></article></main>\n","What can an SEO/GEO audit actually prove? | Audit GEO","/seo-geo-audit");
 const PAGE=html(`<main id="main"><section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">SEO + AI SEARCH FOUNDATIONS</p><h1>Turn website questions<br>into a clear next step.</h1><p>Know what to improve, why it matters, and what to ask your agent to do. A focused website audit, with sources and up to three useful tasks.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#request">Request an audit · €9</a><a class="text-action" href="#example">See what you get</a></div><p class="small">One website. One report. No subscription.<br>We confirm eligibility before asking for payment.</p></div><figure class="hero-visual"><img src="/assets/studio.jpg" srcset="/assets/studio-small.jpg 700w, /assets/studio.jpg 1400w" sizes="(max-width:800px) 100vw, 50vw" width="1400" height="1100" fetchpriority="high" alt="A website open on a laptop in a bright independent studio"><figcaption><strong>Your website. Your agent. A useful next step.</strong><span>A sourced report + a prompt you can put to work.</span></figcaption><div class="offer-stamp"><strong>€9</strong><span>One-off audit<br>No subscription</span></div></figure></section><section class="journey" aria-label="How the audit works"><div><span>01</span><strong>Share your website</strong><p>One public URL. No access to your accounts.</p></div><div><span>02</span><strong>We check for useful work</strong><p>Evidence first. Pay only after eligibility is confirmed.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Give your agent a plan</strong><p>Get a Markdown report and an executable prompt.</p></div></section><section class="section split" id="example"><div><h2>A report you can<br>actually use.</h2><p>Keep it as Markdown, or hand the included prompt to Codex, Claude or your preferred agent with access to your website.</p><div class="demo-actions"><a class="text-action" href="/example.md" download>Download example .md</a><button class="text-action" id="copy-prompt" type="button" style="background:none;border:0;text-decoration:underline">Copy agent prompt</button></div><p id="copy-status" role="status" class="small"></p></div><div><article class="report" aria-label="Illustrative report preview"><div class="file-bar"><span>fieldnote-audit.md</span><span class="tag">Illustrative example</span></div><h2>Evidence. A plan.<br>A way to verify it.</h2><div class="finding"><strong>AI search crawler access</strong><p>A blocked search crawler can limit discovery. Check the real robots.txt against your intended policy.</p></div><div class="finding"><strong>Make the offer easier to understand</strong><p>Explain who your product helps, using factual use cases and clear answers.</p></div><div class="finding"><strong>A title that matches the offer</strong><p>Three conditional tasks, with before/after examples and clear acceptance checks.</p></div><p class="prompt">Evidence register → prioritized tasks<br>Implementation checks → weekly review<br>One complete prompt for your own agent</p><p class="small">Fictional demonstration, not a measured customer result.</p></article><div class="row"><strong>Evidence before advice</strong><p>Public pages, titles, indexing directives and search crawler rules, with sources and explicit unknowns.</p></div><div class="row"><strong>Up to three supported tasks</strong><p>A narrow next step for your own agent. No invented tactics just to fill a report.</p></div><div class="row"><strong>Clear measurement boundaries</strong><p>Technical eligibility is not visibility. We don't claim to measure your Google position or ChatGPT and Claude mentions without the relevant data.</p></div></div></section><section class="section split" id="request"><div><h2>Start with one website.</h2><p class="price">€9<span>one-off pilot price</span></p><p>Send your public website and an email for your request record. You will go straight to a private page to check progress and download your report. This pilot does not send email notifications. We check whether the audit can be useful before you pay.</p><p class="small">The pilot is taking requests. Paid orders open only after eligibility and delivery capacity are confirmed. No automatic charge, no recurring billing.</p></div><form class="form" id="audit-form" action="/api/requests" method="post" aria-label="Audit request"><div class="field"><label for="website">Website to audit (required)</label><input id="website" name="website" type="url" aria-describedby="website-help" placeholder="https://your-website.com" required maxlength="500" autocomplete="url"><p class="small" id="website-help">A public HTTPS website that you own or manage.</p></div><div class="field"><label for="email">Your email (required)</label><input id="email" name="email" aria-describedby="email-help" type="email" placeholder="you@your-company.com" required maxlength="254" autocomplete="email"><p class="small" id="email-help">Stored with your request. No email notifications are sent during this pilot. Save your private status page to access the report.</p></div><div class="trap" aria-hidden="true"><label for="company">Leave this empty</label><input id="company" name="company" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="consent" required><span>I own or manage this website and agree to have these details used to process this audit request. <a href="/privacy">Privacy & scope</a></span></label><button class="button" type="submit">Submit audit request</button><div id="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div></form></section><section class="section"><h2>A few honest answers.</h2><details><summary>Will this make ChatGPT recommend my business?</summary><p>No guarantee. This audit checks your website's foundations and identifies supported improvements. Crawling, citation and recommendation are separate things.</p></details><details><summary>Does it measure my SEO position or LLM visibility?</summary><p>The initial €9 pilot covers technical foundations and actionable content findings. Search Console positions need your export. LLM mention testing needs a declared prompt sample, engine and date; API samples would be labelled separately from the ChatGPT and Claude consumer interfaces.</p></details><details><summary>Can my agent execute the plan each week?</summary><p>Yes, if it can access your repository or CMS. It should verify previous work and new evidence first. Sometimes the right weekly recommendation is to make no change.</p></details><details><summary>When do I pay and receive the report?</summary><p>We first confirm eligibility and a delivery date. You then get a Stripe payment link for €9. A report is released only after payment is verified. This page does not collect payment details.</p></details></section></main><script src="/app.js" defer></script>`,undefined,'/');
 const SCRIPT=`const form=document.querySelector('#audit-form'),status=document.querySelector('#form-status');form.addEventListener('submit',async event=>{event.preventDefault();const button=form.querySelector('button[type=submit]');button.disabled=true;form.setAttribute('aria-busy','true');status.className='notice';status.textContent='Saving your request…';try{const f=new FormData(form);const res=await fetch('/api/requests',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({website:f.get('website'),email:f.get('email'),consent:f.get('consent')==='on',company:f.get('company')})});const data=await res.json();if(!res.ok)throw new Error(data.error||'Unable to save your request. Please try again.');status.replaceChildren();const p=document.createElement('p');p.textContent='Request saved. Keep your private tracking link to check for updates. No payment has been taken.';const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=data.tracking;a.textContent='Open your request';if(typeof data.tracking!=='string'||!new RegExp('^/request/[a-f0-9]{64}$').test(data.tracking))throw new Error('The server did not return a valid tracking link.');status.append(p,a);form.reset();window.location.assign(data.tracking);}catch(error){status.className='notice error';status.textContent=error.message;}finally{button.disabled=false;form.removeAttribute('aria-busy');}});document.querySelector('#copy-prompt').addEventListener('click',async()=>{const o=document.querySelector('#copy-status');try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(${JSON.stringify(AGENT_PROMPT)});o.textContent='Prompt copied. Attach your report before running it.';}catch{o.textContent='Clipboard unavailable. Download the Markdown example to copy its prompt.';}});`;
 const PRIVACY=html(`<main id="main" class="page"><h1>Privacy & scope</h1><p>This pilot stores your email, public website URL, request identifier and processing status solely to handle your audit request. It does not add you to a marketing list. Do not submit passwords, API keys or private URLs.</p><p>Keep your private tracking link secure. It gives access to your request status and, when available, your report. Use the deletion button on that page to withdraw an unpaid request.</p><p>Unpaid requests expire after 30 days. Report data expires after 90 days. Expired data is removed during operator processing or when accessed. Payment records, if any, are held separately by Stripe. No analytics or advertising cookies are used by this application.</p><p>The €9 pilot covers public technical SEO and AI search foundations, a Markdown report and an agent prompt. It does not include guaranteed rankings, consumer LLM visibility scores, private Search Console access, or publishing changes to your website.</p><p>We confirm eligibility, the scope and a delivery date before asking for payment through Stripe under Vutler. No subscription or recurring charge.</p><a class="text-action" href="/">Back to the pilot</a></main>`,'Privacy & scope — Audit GEO','/privacy');
